On Wed, 23 Aug 2006, PotatoVillain@gmail.com wrote:

> I've been playing nethack for a few years off and on, and never
> really gotten a character past level 8, so my recent death in the
> astral plane was an extremely big leap forward for me. Be warned, this
> post is pretty long, and contains spoilers.

Congratulations on your advancement.

Some spoilery comments follow.

> could touch me, except a grey unicorn got stuck behind a boulder and I
> that I left the black unicorn alive, I was dismayed to see that it was
> chaotic.
> level 10, I found a white unicorn and promptly murdered it. It's
> sacrifice converted the altar, and the black unicorn's mollified
> Odin.

You seem to be mixing up the colours of your unicorns. Furthermore, grey
unicorns always are neutral, black are chaotic, white are lawful.

> I started to descend deeper, my bags brimming with unidentified crap
> (even wands - very dangerous).

I hope you did not put unidentified wands in your bag of holding? This is
indeed dangerous, but if your bag survives once putting a particular wand
into it, there is no danger with any wands of that kind.

> I zapped a wand and it changed the engraving to some fortune, so clearly
> this is a wand of enlightenment.

No, it is a wand of polymorph. Writing with wands of enlightenment has the
same effect as zapping.

> At this point, I was still struggling with unidentified scrolls,
> potions, rings, and wands.

Wands are easy to identify. Price identify and unicorn horns help in
sorting the most dangerous scrolls and potions from those safe to try out.
Rings can be identified by putting them into sinks (but mostly they get
lost this way), non-cursed rings can be put on (but check out for
conflict).

> Unfortunately, this cursed one of my bags of holding, and I had to
> evacuate it's contents to the other bag and dump it.

You probably lost some items in this process. You should have made some
holy water by now, so that this was entirely unneccessary.

> I'm working my way up Rodney's tower, and I see a master mind
> flayer. Thinking I am invincible, I attack it and it mind-sucks me.
> Crap. I zap it with a wand of death, it misses, sucks me again, and I
> zap it again and it dies. I try to assess the damage. Not too bad. I
> pull stuff out of my bag and write up a blessed identify scroll hoping
> I can re-identify everything important.

You still had wishes left from the wand. Blessed scrolls of genocide are
very good wishes, as you now know.

> In goes the wand of canceling that got un-identified, blowing up the bag
> and all my reserve gear.

Outch.

> About halfway up through hell, I walk through a door and am hit by a
> potion of paralysis. It was thrown by a master mind flayer. This could
> be bad. He sucks the grease from my hat, and my brain down to int 4
> before I am un-paralyzed. I smack him with my hammer, and continue on,
> thankful I wasn't killed. Shortly after, the mail daemon arrives, and
> someone points out I almost died.

Hey, helpful advice there.

> This was my first real attempt at ascension, and I got really far. I
> figure I had a 1/3 chance of ascending, and would be cheering right now
> if that altar had been neutral. I will try again, in time. If you have
> read the story this far, thanks for listening to the tale of Wahzor the
> Valkyrie, who almost made it. I'm posting this to tell the story, to
> boast a little at how far I got, asking for some advice for next time,
> and perhaps a little sympathy.

You did pretty well. From your tale, you have had some very exciting
battles starting from when you woke up the wizard. Getting to the Astral
Plane after not seeing even the mid-game before is pretty impressive.

> Astral Plane $:109 HP:0(68) Pw:53(53) AC:-17 Xp:17/787962 T:44144 Ill

AC should be improved.

> You never genocided any monsters

Problem. It is OK to spare maybe a single wish for emergencies, but when
you get the castle's wand, burn it on everything useful. A scroll of
genocide would have saved you the mind flayer encounters, and a magic
marker would have helped you with AC, magic mapping, identify and charging
the wand of death.

I think you should focus more on identifying your gear. This takes only
small effort, yet helps you tremendously. Read the identify spoiler to get
all the details, or focus on altars, prices, engraving and unicorn horns
to find out what something is or at the least whether you can try it out
safely.

Also, you did not have a single potion of holy water in your inventory at
the end, and you did not have a bag. Even ordinary bags are extremely
useful to prevent items inside from getting cursed; in particular, the
holy water that you better take with you.


All in all, you know have a better feeling about what to expect on the
run. With better preparation, an ascension is not far away.

